CAT = "chlProcesses"; SEG = "PRC"
Q = [
("A leader is choosing the main reference for steam sterilization practice in the department. Which document fits best?",
 "ANSI/AAMI ST79", ["ANSI/AAMI ST91 only", "The OSHA hazard communication rule", "The hospital's billing manual"],
 "ST79 is the AAMI standard on steam sterilization and sterility assurance in health care facilities, one of the references HSPA lists for the CHL exam."),
("Why might a hospital system move instrument reprocessing to an off-site center?",
 "To pool volume and standardize", ["To end all transport of trays", "To drop the need for tracking", "To loosen the IFU rules at the new site"],
 "Off-site or multi-site reprocessing can centralize equipment and staff and standardize practice, but adds transport, turnaround and tracking demands."),
("What is a key risk a leader must plan for when reprocessing moves off-site?",
 "Transport delays and turnaround", ["Fewer instruments to clean", "No need for sterile storage", "Fewer infection prevention duties"],
 "Moving trays between sites adds travel time, so par levels, transport containers and turnaround agreements must be planned to keep cases on schedule."),
("Before signing with a third-party reprocessing vendor, what should a leader confirm?",
 "They meet the same standards", ["They charge the lowest unit price", "They own the most delivery trucks", "They send no quality reports"],
 "Outsourced work must meet the same standards, regulations and manufacturer instructions as in-house work, with quality reporting built into the contract."),
("What does an instrument tracking system mainly give a department?",
 "Traceability of sets to patients", ["Faster steam sterilizer cycles", "Fully automatic assembly of every tray", "Lower water use for each wash"],
 "Tracking links instruments, sets, loads and patients, which supports recalls, productivity data and case cart accuracy."),
("A surgeon asks to add a robotic system to the OR. What should the SP leader review first?",
 "The device reprocessing IFUs", ["The surgeon's case volume only", "The color of the instrument trays", "The vendor's marketing brochure"],
 "Complex devices like robotic instruments bring their own cleaning, inspection and sterilization requirements that drive equipment, time and training needs."),
("Which statement about standardizing instrument trays is correct?",
 "It reduces errors and saves time", ["It increases the number of sets", "It removes the need for count sheets", "It requires more sterilizers"],
 "Standard trays with fewer unique sets make assembly more consistent, reduce missing-item errors and simplify inventory."),
("Which device is outside surgical instruments but often in SP's scope?",
 "Flexible endoscopes", ["Patient meal trays", "Office printers and copiers", "Nursing call light panels"],
 "The outline lists non-surgical equipment such as endoscopes and ultrasound probes, which need reprocessing oversight even when used in clinics."),
("What does a loaner instrument agreement with a vendor usually set out?",
 "Delivery timing and processing rules", ["The surgeon's salary and bonus", "The patient's insurance coverage terms", "The OR's nurse staffing grid"],
 "Loaner agreements cover when sets arrive before a case, the IFUs and count sheets that come with them, and how sets are returned."),
("Why should loaner sets arrive well before the scheduled case?",
 "So they can be fully reprocessed", ["So the vendor can be paid sooner", "So the case can start earlier", "So staff can skip the count sheet"],
 "Late loaners pressure staff to rush cleaning and sterilization. Early delivery allows full decontamination, inspection, assembly and sterilization."),
("A critical supply is on national backorder. What is a sound leadership response?",
 "Approve substitutes and tell users", ["Keep the shortage from the OR", "Reprocess single-use items", "Cancel every surgery that uses the item"],
 "During shortages leaders work with purchasing, clinicians and infection prevention to approve alternatives and communicate changes."),
("When reviewing an instrument repair contract, what should a leader check?",
 "Turnaround and quality terms", ["The design of the vendor's logo", "Whether it bans our inspection", "How many staff the vendor employs"],
 "Repair contracts should specify turnaround, quality and documentation so instruments come back safe and on time."),
("What does designing a workflow that prevents cross-contamination require?",
 "One-way flow, dirty to clean", ["Shared tables for every task", "Two-way staff and cart traffic", "Sterile storage beside decontamination"],
 "Workflow must move items one way, from decontamination to preparation to sterile storage, in line with standards such as ST79."),
("Which change improves ergonomics in an assembly area?",
 "Adjustable-height workstations", ["Taller fixed shelving along every wall", "Heavier instrument trays", "Longer standing shifts"],
 "Adjustable workstations fit different workers and reduce strain from repeated reaching, bending and lifting."),
("A new washer-disinfector model claims faster cycles. What should the leader confirm before buying?",
 "Its validated cycles fit the devices", ["It is the lowest-cost model offered", "Its color matches the room's design", "It needs no preventive maintenance at all"],
 "Equipment must have validated cycles compatible with the department's devices and the device IFUs, plus utility and maintenance needs."),
("Why is the cycle count of a sterilizer tracked?",
 "To plan maintenance and replacement", ["To bill each cycle to a patient", "To limit staff overtime hours", "To set the sterile storage shelf life"],
 "Cycle counts show how hard equipment works, guiding preventive maintenance schedules and end-of-life replacement planning."),
("Which records support an equipment replacement plan?",
 "Age, repairs and downtime", ["The color of each machine", "Which staff members like it", "Only the date it was installed"],
 "Repair frequency, downtime, cost of upkeep and age help a leader decide when replacing equipment is safer and cheaper."),
("What does preventive maintenance of reprocessing equipment do?",
 "Prevents breakdowns", ["Replaces cleaning verification", "Removes the need for IFUs", "Lets cycles skip monitoring"],
 "Scheduled maintenance by qualified people keeps equipment within its specifications and reduces unplanned breakdowns."),
("Why do autoclaves need routine chamber and drain cleaning?",
 "Residue can harm loads and the unit", ["It changes the cycle temperature", "It replaces the need for biological indicators", "It makes the chamber lighter"],
 "Debris and mineral buildup can stain instruments, block drains and affect performance, so cleaning follows the manufacturer's schedule."),
("Which utility most affects final rinse quality in reprocessing?",
 "Water quality", ["Lighting levels", "Phone lines", "Parking capacity"],
 "Water that is too hard or contaminated can leave residue or microbes, so water quality is monitored as part of reprocessing."),
("What does a water management program in a health care facility address?",
 "Growth of waterborne germs", ["Water bills for each unit", "Bottled drinking water for staff", "Rain runoff from the roof"],
 "Water management programs reduce the growth and spread of waterborne pathogens such as Legionella in building water systems."),
("Why are HVAC settings monitored in sterile processing?",
 "Airflow and humidity affect safety", ["To save money on staff uniforms", "To keep radio reception clear", "To set the sterilizer cycle times each day"],
 "Pressure relationships, temperature and humidity in each area affect contamination control and packaging integrity."),
("What does environment of care mean for an SP leader?",
 "A safe, compliant physical setting", ["The staff holiday schedule", "Patient meal planning and delivery", "The hospital's logo design"],
 "Environment of care covers the building, equipment, utilities and safety systems that must meet accreditation and regulatory standards."),
("A leader learns AI tools are being marketed for instrument identification. What is the right first step?",
 "Evaluate evidence and fit first", ["Buy it before other hospitals do", "Replace all inspection staff with it", "Ignore all new technology"],
 "New technology is assessed for proven benefit, compatibility with workflows and standards, and cost before adoption."),
]
